Theorem RL-T2: Compositional placement soundness over the CFG ledger

  Preconditions:
    - The CFG-ledger model: blocks carry instruction lists; directed edges
      carry a kind (normal, back-edge, unwind); a TRMC-rewritten tail-call
      region marker names the loop blocks a self-recursive tail call became.
      A walk is an entry-anchored, edge-connected, exit-terminated block
      sequence; the declarative walk predicate covers EVERY walk, including
      one crossing a back-edge arbitrarily many times, and the fuel-bounded
      enumeration (fuel-bounded recursion, no termination measure) is proven
      sound against it - every enumerated walk is a genuine CFG walk.
    - Partition classes are the T1 union-find representatives (the
      buildPartitionUF / find executable from the partition module); the
      engine takes the partition AS GIVEN input and admits no phi edge of
      its own. Class equality is provably the T1 sameRep verdict.
    - Events are DERIVED per class by a computed classification over
      instruction-shaped input, never free input: BIRTH (fresh allocation,
      +1), CREDIT (RL-1 duplication inc or cross-class jump-arg handoff in,
      +1), CONSUME (a PLACED release, an RL-2 ownership-transferring
      terminal use per the committed twelve-kind table, or a cross-class
      jump-arg handoff out, -1), READ (Project borrow-view read or an RL-2
      non-transferring terminal read; requires a live count), MUTATE (RL-7
      dynamic-COW mutation carrying its live-sibling floor, computed from
      the path suffix as the number of distinct same-class sibling values
      still read later). A jump arg whose receiving block-param is in the
      SAME class is the RL-4 exemption - no ledger event; the reference
      persists in the class across the edge.
    - The placement under verification is the set of placed releases
      (burden decs) in the instruction stream; the three-clause invariant
      is checked per class per path: (1) the class's ledger nets zero;
      (2) the running count is at least 1 at every READ; (3) the running
      count is at least 1 + live-siblings at every dynamic-COW MUTATE.
    - The compiled Lean model is the calculus authority for the placement
      invariant; conformance of the shipped emitter to the model is
      established empirically on the compiler's ARC-verified test surface,
      not discharged here.

  Soundness property:
    Forall CFG (back-edges, unwind edges, TRMC regions included), forall
    partition-class map, forall walk, forall class: a placement whose
    derived per-class ledger satisfies the three clauses on every walk is
    balanced-and-safe on EVERY walk - no leak (net 0), no use-after-free
    (the count floor holds at every READ), no COW corruption (the sibling
    floor holds at every MUTATE). The declarative three-clause check is
    EXACTLY the operational guarantee (both directions), so a placement
    violating any clause on any path is provably rejected: a release
    relocated past a multi-predecessor merge double-frees the predecessor
    path on which the class is already dead; a release placed before a
    later READ frees early; an early sibling release before a dynamic-COW
    mutate corrupts the live sibling; a release placed after the TRMC
    tail-call transfer double-frees the transferred accumulator.

  Proof obligation:
    (P1) Classification grounding. The derived terminal-use event matches
         the committed RL-2 twelve-kind table verdict for every kind:
         CONSUME exactly on the 9 ownership-transfer kinds, READ on the 3
         non-transfer kinds. Jump-arg routing consumes the partition: a
         same-class receiving param is the RL-4 exemption (no event); a
         cross-class param is a handoff (consume from the source class,
         credit into the param class). Class equality is the T1 union-find
         sameRep verdict - the classes ARE the T1 representatives.
    (P2) Clauses-safety equivalence. A class's per-path ledger satisfies
         the three clauses EXACTLY when its operational run is
         balanced-and-safe: the running count is the start plus the net
         ledger (fold lemma); the hazard flags are sticky; the floor
         clauses hold from a start count exactly when the run from that
         count raises neither flag (induction on the event list); clause 1
         is the no-leak surface, clause 2 the use-after-free surface,
         clause 3 the COW-corruption surface.
    (P3) THE compositional placement theorem. For every CFG, every
         partition-class map, and every walk of the declarative predicate,
         the three-clause hypothesis yields balanced-and-safe - plus the
         fuel-bounded enumeration corollary, and enumeration soundness
         (every enumerated walk is a genuine walk: head at the entry,
         edge-connected suffix, exit-terminated).
    (P4) Kill-criterion K1 - unwind-fed multi-predecessor merge. On the CFG
         whose merge block has two predecessors, one arriving via an UNWIND
         edge, with the class member DEAD on the unwind path (the cleanup
         released it) and LIVE through the normal path: the cured
         path-local placement satisfies all three clauses on BOTH
         enumerated walks and is balanced-and-safe for EVERY class (the
         touched class by computation over the real union-find, every
         untouched class by the empty-ledger lemma). The past-merge
         relocation is REJECTED: the unwind path nets -1 (double free)
         while the normal path alone still balances - only the per-class
         PER-PATH invariant catches it. Releases are path-local, never
         past a merge.
    (P5) Kill-criterion K2 - TRMC-marked back-edge loop, every iteration
         count. On the loop CFG (back-edge latch to header, TRMC region
         marker on header + body) with a loop-invariant collection class
         (T1 tier-1 view edge, singleton-witness-admitted) and a
         loop-carried accumulator whose header block-param is its OWN class
         (distinct birth-sites - the T1 kill-criterion refuses the phi):
         the n-iteration walk is a genuine CFG walk crossing the back-edge
         exactly n times, and EVERY touched class satisfies all three
         clauses for EVERY n, by the prefix / n-fold net-zero cycle /
         suffix decomposition (the running count re-enters each iteration
         at the loop invariant) - no termination hand-waving, no unrolled
         approximation. A release placed AFTER the tail-call ownership
         transfer inside the TRMC region is REJECTED (nets -1) - the RL-34
         no-post-tail-call-dec law at the ledger level.
    (P6) Negative witnesses. The PRE-READ RELEASE (a release placed before
         a later READ on the same class/path) is REJECTED: the ledger nets
         zero - clause 1 alone would pass - but the READ fires at count 0
         (clause 2 false; the operational machine observes the
         use-after-free). The EARLY SIBLING RELEASE before a dynamic-COW
         MUTATE is REJECTED, and clause 3 is the ONLY clause that sees it:
         net zero passes clause 1, the sibling's later read still sees
         count 1 so clause 2 passes, but the mutate fires at count 1
         against a floor of 2 (the COW-corruption surface); the cured
         placement holding the sibling credit live across the mutate
         satisfies all three clauses.
    (P7) Kill-criterion K3 - TRMC ContextHole hole-fill (release-after-fill).
         The instruction alphabet carries `holeFill v hole` - the TRMC
         fill-at-recursive-call: v's reference transfers INTO aggregate
         `hole`'s interior (a consume on v's class - the ConstructArg
         analogy; interior accounting is T6/PV-6's concern) and the
         unconditional in-place hole write carries the clause-3
         live-sibling floor on `hole`'s class (mutate event, suffix-derived
         sibling count; TRMC unique-context makes the floor trivially
         satisfiable - the model still checks it). The kill criterion: a
         placed release of v AFTER its hole-fill double-releases - the
         derived ledger [birth, consume, consume] nets -1, clause 1
         REJECTS (cross-class and same-class both pinned). The CURED
         placement plans NO dec after the fill - the fill IS v's release
         ([birth, consume] nets 0). Clause 2 stays live (a terminal read of
         the filled value after its fill observes a drained count -
         rejected); clause 3 stays live for the fill write (a live sibling
         read after the fill raises the floor to 2 - a single birth fails).
         The same-class self-referential fill (the linked-node chain - one
         static birth site per T1) balances: two births, mutate + consume
         at the fill, one onward transfer.

